Z||000036||GT-maniac||11-22-2001||06:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Nice pics and cars..but WHAT IN THE HELL HAPPENED TO THAT INDY? NO NO NO...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well the guy that owned it claimed it was a basket case when he got it and couldn't restore it. I personally wasn't that crazy about it as I didn't like the spoilers or the racing stickers all over it. It was interesting though and was apparently pretty quick. Had a V6 with some kind of dual carbuerator setup in it. Didn't actually see it as he was reluctant to open the hatch for some reason. Sounded pretty mean.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000037||The Fieromaster||11-23-2001||03:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTMike:<BR><B>whats a fiero gtp????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>GTP was the never released 89 Fiero.. NOT the grey one BUT the red one... screw it ill post a pic below... There were no GTP Fieros ever released  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  But i have heard all kinds of different engines that were supposed to be in the car.. dunno for sure what was!?<BR>Ok here is the real 89 GTP... sorry if pics are too big!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/89Fproto_(1).jpg"> <BR>Here is proof it WAS a GTP.. just look at the back wall of the "car show booth" setup!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Magazine_Page62.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
